  "notes": [
    "The book divides the list into Early (1807-1808), Middle (1809-1811) and Late (1812-1814) periods. The builder doesn't enforce them: choices that belong to a period say so in their name.",
    "Period limits that differ: Veteran (Elite 5+) is open to any battalion in the Middle period but up to half in the Early and Late, where Elite 4+ isn't offered; in the Middle period take one or the other. In the Early period any battalion can be Large and any regiment Light (rather than one per brigade).",
    "The Cavalry Brigade takes 2-3 Dragoons with up to one Chasseur regiment (Early), or 2-4 Hussars or Chasseurs with up to one Dragoon regiment (Middle, Late), plus up to one Vistula Lancer regiment in the army (Early, Middle); the builder checks the Vistula Lancers but not the Dragoon and light mix.",
    "The Guard Cavalry Brigade also needs a Cavalry Brigade; the builder checks the 3 infantry brigades.",
    "Combined Grenadiers and Voltigeurs: a brigade's battalions can lose their Grenadier/Carabinier companies (and 1 Hand-to-Hand) or Voltigeur companies (and Mixed Formation). Two battalions' companies make a Tiny unit, three a Small unit, four a standard one; a battalion that loses both becomes Small. Not built here, beyond the Reserve brigade's Combined Grenadier battalions.",
    "Foreign formations: upgrades and downgrades in the Infantry Brigade can stand for Swiss, Irish, Hanoverian, Nassau, Baden, Hesse-Darmstadt and Legion du Midi troops. Italians use the French stat lines without Pas de Charge.",
    "Dismounted Dragoons (p. 68): a Dragoon regiment can start the game dismounted, as a Small infantry unit (4/2/4/3, Skirmish). Not built here.",
    "The chapter gives Combined Grenadiers Shooting 4 (p. 66) and Vistula Lancers Reliable (p. 71); the list's table (p. 106) is followed.",
    "Half batteries cost half points, rounded up (Foot 14, Horse 11), with the half battery stat line on p. 107 (2-1-1, Stamina 1).",
    "Named commanders have no official points cost in this supplement; they're priced here at the Divisional Commander cost for their Staff Rating, so adjust as you agree."
  ],
